- A * marks a secret. Read it through its $ENV name; never inline a value.
- For a negative flow (error asserted), derive the invalid value from the env value plus "-wrong"; never reuse the valid one.
- Page objects are TypeScript classes taking \`page: Page\`; expose locators as getters.
- Use \`getByLabel\`/\`getByRole\`/\`getByTestId\` for the matching strategies; raw \`page.locator\` only for css/xpath.
- Use web-first assertions (\`await expect(locator).toBeVisible()\`); never \`waitForTimeout\`.
- When a locator fails, try its ~ fallbacks in rank order, then match @fp (role, label, near, path, a=) against the page.
- Return a replacement only when it resolves to a single element; otherwise report the element as unrecoverable.
@task
Write Playwright (TypeScript) tests (P1=pages/LoginPage.ts, scenario=tests/login-flow.spec.ts). Run npx playwright test until green. For a failing element id, answer {"el":"eN","loc":"strategy:value"} with the best replacement.
"
`;

